 ### Opacity Field Estimation for Detection
 - **Definition**: Opacity field models scene geometry as probability of object presence (1.0 if opaque) [S4].
-- **Step**: Share the G-MLP learned in the NeRF branch with the detection branch. Input augmented volume features of 3D detection into the shared G-MLP [S4]. Transform density to opacity. Since ray direction and point distance are undefined in the undirected volume, exploit uniform voxel distribution to cancel constant $\delta_t$. Compute opacity: $\alpha(\mathbf{p}) = 1 - \exp(-\sigma(\mathbf{p}))$ [S4]. Multiply opacity field with feature grid for 3D detection: $\alpha(\mathbf{p}) \times V_{avg}(\mathbf{p})$ [S4].
+- **Step**: Share the G-MLP learned in the NeRF branch with the detection branch. Input augmented volume features of 3D detection into the shared G-MLP [S4]. Transform density to opacity. Since ray direction and point distance are undefined in the undirected volume, exploit uniform voxel distribution to cancel constant $\delta_t$ [S4]. Compute opacity: $\alpha(\mathbf{p}) = 1 - \exp(-\sigma(\mathbf{p}))$ [S4]. Multiply opacity field with feature grid for 3D detection: $\alpha(\mathbf{p}) \times V_{avg}(\mathbf{p})$ [S4].
