 ### GP-NeRF
 - **Definition**: A unified learning framework that embeds NeRF and 2D segmentation modules to perform context-aware 3D scene perception, jointly constructing radiance and semantic-embedding fields and facilitating joint volumetric rendering [S6].
-- **Step**: 1. Extract reference features $F^{\text{sem}}_i$ using a Multi-Scale Feature Extractor. 2. Use Field Aggregation Transformer to co-aggregate radiance and semantic-embedding fields. 3. Use Ray Aggregation Transformer to render them jointly in novel views. 4. Feed rendered rich-semantic features $S^{2D}_{\text{sem}}$ into a Context-Aware Perception Head (2D segmentation module) for context-aware perception. 5. Optimize jointly with RGB loss, instance loss, semantic loss, and two self-distillation losses [S6].
-- **Comparison**: Differs from prior methods (Semantic-NeRF, Semantic-Ray) that render semantic labels/features per pixel independently. GP-NeRF renders rich-semantic features and feeds them to a 2D segmentation module for context-aware perception, ensuring geometry distribution consistency between radiance and semantic fields [S6].
+- **Step**: 1. Extract reference features $F^{\text{sem}}_i$ using a Multi-Scale Feature Extractor [G]. 2. Use Field Aggregation Transformer to co-aggregate radiance and semantic-embedding fields [G]. 3. Use Ray Aggregation Transformer to render them jointly in novel views [G]. 4. Feed rendered rich-semantic features $S^{2D}_{\text{sem}}$ into a Context-Aware Perception Head (2D segmentation module) for context-aware perception [G]. 5. Optimize jointly with RGB loss, instance loss, semantic loss, and two self-distillation losses [G].
